# Decided
- Claude's draft put every header as an @file block; trueqbit: a file
  whose reason one construct carries takes the header on that
  construct's doc-comment, the @file block staying for the node headers
  of ast/ and schema/ (an internal node struct with a public factory,
  often a family) and for grouping files. Recorded in campaign.md
  "Form".
- cte_column_names_collector.h was named in the singular, after the
  collector, which does one of three steps; the reason is borne by
  resolve_cte_column_names. Claude leaned for an @file header;
  trueqbit offered cte_column_names_collecting.h or cte_column_names.h.
  Claude's lean, taken: cte_column_names.h - "collecting" narrows the
  name to step 1 again.
- History read (git log --follow): ae87b11a combined the collector into
  one constexpr-if dispatch, 8e9f0b59 looked up an asterisk's table by
  its mapped type, 0acd384c (note: the include of column_lookup.h it
  calls). No commit chose the name for a reason beyond the collector.
- Pure rename: the file at 100% similarity; cte_db_objects.h and
  statement_serializer.h change their include line; the amalgamation
  differs in the two include comments alone. TODO.md, docs/, AGENTS.md,
  .claude/skills/ and the amalgamation manifests name no old path.

# Discussed
Green: pre-commit.sh 0; clang-format 20 unchanged; no "on purpose:".
The token streams differ by the include lines, as a rename makes them.
pre-commit.sh amalgamates before it formats: a run on a tree whose
includes clang-format then re-sorts leaves a stale amalgamation - a
second run fixed it here (the reverse sed of the split left storage.h
unsorted for one run).

